                <pb facs="0171" n="65" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg65"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pacheco to Mr. Blaine</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States in Central America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1891-06-09"><hi rendition="#italic">June 9,
                                1891</hi>.</date> (Received June 25.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 28.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your instructions numbered 32, of February 20, and 44, of March 16, 1891,
                    relative to a <pb facs="0172" n="66" xml:id="pg66"/> system of cable
                    communication between Washington and this legation, and to report that I have
                    addressed a letter to the minister of foreign affairs of Salvador requesting a
                    thorough investigation of the matter with a view to prevent a recurrence of the
                    interference with cable communication in the hope that the Government of
                    Salvador will speedily apply a remedy in furtherance of Central American
                    interests no less than of those of the United States.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. Pacheco</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
